 "centralFinding": {
  "claim": "The cluster's two literatures are DISJOINT at the instrument boundary. No source in 55 both reads FCM and measures boredom with EEG or eye-tracking.",
  "verifiedBy": [
   {
    "route": "construct-based",
    "detail": "22 units treat profound boredom; 19 units carry a hard instrument (EEG/pupil/gaze/blink/ML). Intersection: EMPTY."
   },
   {
    "route": "bridge-based",
    "detail": "21 units carry a bridges-to-fcm edge; 19 units carry a hard-instrument operationalizes-measure edge. Intersection: EMPTY. Unit-ID ranges barely touch: FCM-bridging = bor-sec-01..18 (+23,48,51,54,55); hard-instrumented = bor-sec-21..41."
   }
  ],
  "consequence": "The three FCM-form rows are reachable by self-report and nothing else -- and self-report is the one instrument the phenomenological tradition says cannot in principle access an attunement (fcm-03, awakened not ascertained; bor-sec-48) and the one the empirical literature shows does not correlate with any physiological signature (bor-sec-28, null correlation, N=13).",
  "sharpestCell": "profound boredom x self-report is populated by bor-sec-04 -- Elpidorou & Freeman -- whose whole argument is that BPS/ZBS do NOT measure profound boredom (pp.9-15). The cell exists because they discuss the instruments, not because the instruments work.",
  "honestReading": "(P/anticipatory-application) This concordance documents a GAP, not a bridge. Part III cannot cite it as showing the literatures converge. Part III's own cross-cutting design has no precedent in these 55 sources -- and this grid is the evidence for that claim.",
  "provenance": "P/anticipatory-application"
 },
